    "media:imagetext": "TWA-Transcontinental and Western Air, Inc.\nDouglas DC-4\nOriginally built as military C-54s, eight Skymasters were\nreleased to TWA in late 1945. Supplementing the Constella-\ntion fleet on overseas routes, the DC-4s inaugurated service\nto Cairo in 1946. As more Connies were delivered, the\nSkymasters also served all-cargo runs. Eventually they flew\npassenger and freighter flights solely within the United\nStates, and all were retired by 1961. TWA operated a total of\neighteen DC-4s, naming them for points of interest on its\nsystem. Shown on this card is \"The Acropolis.\nPublished by Aviation World, Inc., P.O. Box 188, Bethel, Conn. 06801 U.S.A.\nD-005\n55788-D\npost card\nPhoto courtesy of Trans World Airlines\nN45346 C/N 27350\n2002.113.474",
